{number: 135}
{title: I am Coming to the Cross}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] I am coming to the cross;
I am [C] poor, and weak, and [G] blind;
I am counting all but dross,
I shall [D7] full salvation [G] find.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G] I am trusting, Lord, in Thee,
Blessed [C] Lamb of Calva-[G] ry;
Humbly at Thy cross I bow,
Save me, [D7] Jesus, save me [G] now.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] Long my heart has sighed for Thee,
Long has [C] evil reigned with-[G] in;
Jesus sweetly speaks to me:
"I will [D7] cleanse you from all [G] sin."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Here I give my all to Thee,
Friends, and [C] time, and earthly [G] store;
Soul and body Thine to be,
Wholly [D7] Thine for ever-[G] more.
{end_of_verse}
